Author:     kairos-code-dev <ulalax@kairoscode.dev>
AuthorDate: Mon Nov 9 16:22:59 2026 +0900
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Mon Nov 9 07:22:59 2026 +0000

    fix(core): admit a complete multipart record on an empty queue (#4118) (#4135)
    
    A DONTWAIT multipart sent through the generic per-frame path (ROUTER,
    DEALER, reply) applied the empty-queue exception only to the final
    frame, so a record whose MORE prefix exceeded a small HWM was refused
    forever even on an empty queue. Callers that hold every part now pass
    pipe_write_complete_record, and write_message_unlocked extends the
    existing exception to that record's MORE frames per spec
    06-auto-hwm :476. Eligibility stays fixed before the first frame,
    MAXMSGSIZE is still checked first, and the incremental decoder rule
    (:470-474) is unchanged.
    
    The two boolean write arguments become one pipe_write_mode_t, and the
    unreachable MAXMSGSIZE reclassification in the HWM refusal branch is
    removed.
    
    Fixes #4118
    
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9jfewPT9LTVRsk1VFWTdu
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

